@import { decisions_load } from "./_partials/_decisions.mds"
@import "./_partials/_settings.mds" as settings
# Self-Review Command

## Usage

/self-review              (auto-detect changed files from git)
/self-review <file>...    (review specific files)

## Phases

### Phase 0: Context Gathering

<!-- curation:on -->
**Produces:** FILES_CHANGED, TASK_DESCRIPTION, DECISIONS_CONTEXT, FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE, FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE_RULES, HEAD_BEFORE
<!-- curation:off -->
**Produces:** FILES_CHANGED, TASK_DESCRIPTION, FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE, FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE_RULES, HEAD_BEFORE
<!-- curation:end -->

Detect changed files and build context:

1. If arguments provided, use those as FILES_CHANGED
2. Else run `git diff --name-only HEAD` + `git diff --name-only --cached` to get staged + unstaged
3. If no changes found, report "No changes to review" and exit
4. Build TASK_DESCRIPTION from recent commit messages or branch name
5. Record `HEAD_BEFORE` (`git rev-parse HEAD`) now, before Polish runs — Phase 3 compares against it

{{settings.settings_resolve()}}

{{decisions_load()}}
<!-- curation:on -->
Pass `DECISIONS_CONTEXT` to the Harden agent only. The Polish agent takes no decisions.

<!-- curation:end -->
{{knowledge_load()}}

Pass `FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE_RULES` to Harden agent.

### Phase 1: Polish agent (Code Refinement)

**Produces:** POLISH_COMMITS
**Requires:** FILES_CHANGED, TASK_DESCRIPTION

Spawn Polish agent to refine code for clarity and consistency:

Agent(subagent_type="Polish", run_in_background=false):
"TASK_DESCRIPTION: {task_description}
FILES_CHANGED: {files_changed}
Polish and refine the code for clarity and consistency while preserving functionality.
Commit any improvements with a conventional-commit message."

### Phase 2: Harden agent (9-Pillar Quality Gate)

**Produces:** HARDEN_STATUS
<!-- curation:on -->
**Requires:** FILES_CHANGED, TASK_DESCRIPTION, DECISIONS_CONTEXT
<!-- curation:off -->
**Requires:** FILES_CHANGED, TASK_DESCRIPTION
<!-- curation:end -->

Spawn Harden agent for quality evaluation and fixing:

Agent(subagent_type="Harden", run_in_background=false):
"TASK_DESCRIPTION: {task_description}
FILES_CHANGED: {files_changed}
<!-- curation:on -->
DECISIONS_CONTEXT: {decisions_context}
<!-- curation:end -->
FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE: {feature_knowledge_rules}
Evaluate against 9-pillar framework. Fix P0/P1 issues. Return structured report.
<!-- curation:on -->
Follow devflow:apply-decisions to scan DECISIONS_CONTEXT and Read full ADR/PF bodies on demand. Skip if (none).
<!-- curation:end -->
Follow devflow:apply-feature-knowledge for FEATURE_KNOWLEDGE. Skip if (none)."

Extract: STATUS (PASS|FIXED|BLOCKED) from the `### Status` line

### Phase 3: Conditional Validation

**Produces:** VALIDATION_RESULT
**Requires:** HEAD_BEFORE, HARDEN_STATUS

If STATUS is BLOCKED, skip this phase: the report (Phase 4) names the blocker.

Run this phase only if HEAD moved — `git rev-parse HEAD` differs from `HEAD_BEFORE`, meaning Polish or Harden committed (Polish alone counts, whatever Harden's STATUS is). Otherwise skip it.

Agent(subagent_type="Validate", run_in_background=false):
"FILES_CHANGED: {output of `git diff --name-only HEAD_BEFORE..HEAD`}
VALIDATION_SCOPE: changed-only
Run build, typecheck, lint, test on modified files"

**If FAIL:** Report validation failures to user and halt
**If PASS:** Continue to report
**Any other or missing Status** (BLOCKED included): report the status or "none", its cause and log path if any, then halt.

### Phase 4: Report

**Requires:** HARDEN_STATUS, VALIDATION_RESULT

Display summary:

## Self-Review Complete

**Files Reviewed**: {n}
**Status**: {PASS|FIXED|BLOCKED}

### Polish agent
- {n} files refined for clarity

### Harden agent (9-Pillar Evaluation)
| Pillar | Status |
|--------|--------|
| Design | {status} |
| Functionality | {status} |
| Security | {status} |
| Complexity | {status} |
| Error Handling | {status} |
| Tests | {status} |
| Naming | {status} |
| Consistency | {status} |
| Documentation | {status} |

### Commits Created
- {sha} {message}

{If BLOCKED: ### Blocking Issue\n{description}}

{{knowledge_writeback_after_load()}}

## Edge Cases

| Case | Handling |
|------|----------|
| Harden agent BLOCKED | Report blocking issue, halt workflow |
| Not in git repo | Report error, suggest running in git repo |

## Principles

1. **Orchestration only** - Command spawns agents, doesn't do the work
2. **Honest reporting** - Display actual agent outputs
3. **Fail fast** - Stop on BLOCKED or a Validate status other than PASS
